</div></section>
<section class="section section--cream"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="section-head reveal" style="justify-content:center;text-align:center"><div><p class="eyebrow">Questions</p><h2>Courtyard FAQs</h2></div></div>
  <div class="faq"><details class="reveal"><summary>How much does courtyard garden design cost?</summary><div class="answer"><p>Design fees depend on the size and complexity of the space. A small courtyard can often be designed in a single, focused package covering the survey, layout and planting plan. Build costs vary mostly with the choice of paving and any structural work. We give a fixed design quote after the first visit.</p></div></details><details class="reveal"><summary>Can you design a courtyard that gets almost no sun?</summary><div class="answer"><p>Yes. Many of the most beautiful courtyards are in deep shade. The key is choosing woodland plants and shade-tolerant evergreens, using pale materials to bounce light and keeping the layout uncluttered.</p></div></details><details class="reveal"><summary>Do courtyard gardens need much maintenance?</summary><div class="answer"><p>A well-planned courtyard needs very little: a seasonal tidy, feeding and occasional pruning of climbers. We can design for automatic irrigation if the space is mostly containers.</p></div></details></div>
</div></section>
